      <memberdef kind="function" id="net_2server_2xpm__pldevice__plat_8c_1ab22e828782eae76cb27df590adce836d" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>XStatus</type>
        <definition>XStatus XPmPlDevice_RebuildDdrmcValidationList</definition>
        <argsstring>(void)</argsstring>
        <name>XPmPlDevice_RebuildDdrmcValidationList</name>
        <param>
          <type>void</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Rebuild the DDRMC validation list from the device database. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS on success, error code otherwise</para></simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>The list is normally filled in by PldMemCtrlrMap() when the PL design CDO is processed. An in-place PLM update does not touch the PL, so that CDO never runs again, and the list starts out empty in the new PLM. Rebuild it here from the DDRMC nodes, which the update does restore, so that DDR addresses keep validating after an update.</para></simplesect>
Every DDRMC node that is present gets added, not just the ones the PL design CDO described. A node that was never described has no address regions, so it makes no difference to validation. </para>        </detaileddescription>
